The Witcher 3 is dropping its first paid  expansion next month while Bethesda are  already talking DLC plans for fall out  for and destinies of the taken King just  hit shelves while DLC packs and  expansions are fairly controversial  there are certainly some gems in the  bunch said gems range from contained  story-based dlc like left behind for the  last of us to massive expansions like  the shivering isles for oblivion or  civilization 5 brave new world there are  also content expansions like episodes  from liberty city for GTA 4 and skyrim  dragonborn which reinvigorated the  massive open worlds of skyrim and  liberty city there are too many great  expansions to mention in this video but  here are five that are among the very  best  Bioshock Infinite's burial at sea dlc  was absolutely fantastic but in the  scope of bioshock dlc it's Minerva's Den  2 Bioshock 2 that wins out Bioshock 2  may have not been everybody's cup of tea  but minerva's den seemed to universally  impress those who played it Minerva's  Den casts you in the role of an alpha  series Big Daddy the game explores  rapture central computing the home of  the thinker otherwise known as the  world's first artificial intelligence  minerva's den earned critical acclaim  for exploring its compelling themes with  expert storytelling and great writing  written by the same guy who would go on  to create gone home minerva's den has a  great story for you to unravel and it's  just as enjoyable as it was in the first  game when it comes to Mass Effect  although the citadel dlc is definitely  awesome it's not my pick for this video  I could have chosen any number of  brilliant DLC packs for the ethic RPG  series but I have to go with lair of the  shadow broker and not just because liara  with my shepherds one true love and she  had a real lonely time without her in  mass effect 2 lair of the shadow broker  only clocks in at a few hours but its  space know our story hilarious meta  banter and incredible assault on the  shadow brokers base they get a must-play  for Mass Effect fans as it seriously  evident from the elder scrolls and  fallout series but there's to really  know what they're doing when it comes to  making DLC for an open world game one of  the best examples of this is old world  blues / Fallout New Vegas old world  blues is the third add-on for new vegas  it sets the tone by having the career  abducted from a drive-in in the new  Vegas wasteland they then need to rescue  their own brain which was removed after  that whole messy abduction thing you'll  encounter lasers and robot scorpions as  well as retro futuristic characters  nuclear disasters hilarious  circumstances and more mutations than  you can shake a stim pack at another  content atom which is popular for very  good reason is tiny tina's assault on  dragon keep for Borderlands 2 it's  fairly well known that the borderlands  universe is totaling bombastic and more  than a little insane tiny tina's  expansion takes that to the next level  with spot on comedy and plenty of  outlandish developments to get you  invested in the characters and the plot  the world of borderlands and its many  inhabitants are reinvented as a figment  of tiny tina's imagination as a result  the campaign adopts a Dungeons and  Dragons style which is reflected in  enemies items and even some brand new  fantasy themed character heads in  typical Borderlands fashion the  absurdity crude humor and clever writing  of this DLC makes any tina's assault on  dragon keep absolutely worth playing red  dead redemption had absolutely nothing  to prove after gathering critical  acclaim nonetheless rockstar was still  set to impress with their DLC undead  nightmare no one anticipated that a game  lauded for its mature and serious  Western story would come out with the  DLC expansion all about shooting up Lum  bees even less of us anticipated that it  would actually be really really good  John marstons main threat shifted for  more men to the zombie plague in the  standalone adventure undead nightmare  which takes place completely separately  to that of the main game fighting off  the undead plague was a fun comedic  departure from the original game  particularly with returning characters  like Seth and the blunderbuss that uses  zombie bits for ammo because of course  it does it was a huge risk to change  gears from complex storytelling to a  pulpy zombie Rob but luckily for rock  star they totally made it work let me  know down in that comment section what's  been your favorite piece of DLC or  expansion pack and do let me know if  there's anything I missed out on I will  get you again next week
 

